h car makers like Mercedes and shipyards among the companies impacted. Meanwhile, a Berlin hospital fire leaves many injured. Follow DW.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Is rule-breaking contagious? The bad apple effect explained</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0078c1d9efa5c276119d5d92d3e39b22263e7f3f399bfbc647fa5627412d92bc</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:55:35Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T06:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-rule-breaking-contagious-the-bad-apple-effect-explained/a-79980025--2bf7f79ae276.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-rule-breaking-contagious-the-bad-apple-effect-explained/a-79980025?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Seeing someone break a rule makes people more likely to break it too, a new study finds, especially when the rule-breaker is on their side politically. Watching others behave well barely made a difference.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey: Thousands protest closure of critical media outlets</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:95526ec9abb8ae3a3e8a52732c3fbbcc30f9fc805e37e5e8b5c90da09198fb1b</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:32Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T21:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/turkey-thousands-protest-closure-of-critical-media-outlets/a-80015347--7bbb07b22139.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turkey-thousands-protest-closure-of-critical-media-outlets/a-80015347?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Protesters gathered in Istanbul to show their support for press freedom in Turkey. The protest was called just days after the police raided Sozcu TV and arrested several senior staff members.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Sudan: Drones hit UN building, residential area in Khartoum</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b5efec7f436fd2e32cbc89b3d147d368053d24a74301ca2cca8f6211567179bd</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:32Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T19:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/sudan-drones-hit-un-building-residential-area-in-khartoum/a-80015122--86bdbc88b2b0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/sudan-drones-hit-un-building-residential-area-in-khartoum/a-80015122?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The drones targeted Khartoum, damaging a UN building in the residential area. The UN agency deemed it unacceptable that humanitarian workers were exposed to such danger.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Libya: Suspected drone attack hits Russian ship in Benghazi</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:589a34b82259f04e822c2a22da23ca47258624fc7b931bee9b526d80b35ddf69</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:32Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T16:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/libya-suspected-drone-attack-hits-russian-ship-in-benghazi/a-80014545--a60ea6375dca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/libya-suspected-drone-attack-hits-russian-ship-in-benghazi/a-80014545?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Russian vessel at an eastern Libyan naval base was hit by what is suspected to be a drone strike.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Israel's Eisenkot condemns 'Jewish terrorism' in West Bank</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0f4ce47cc69913b43c2116c6fa7cfd91db1526e770428dfa38f91da254d34d62</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:32Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T15:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/israel-s-eisenkot-condemns-jewish-terrorism-in-west-bank/a-80013861--f4c08d0b63d1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/israel-s-eisenkot-condemns-jewish-terrorism-in-west-bank/a-80013861?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Israeli opposition leader Gadi Eisenkot has condemned a recent series of arson attacks in the occupied West Bank as "Jewish terrorism." Israeli authorities have opened an investigation into the incidents.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>COP31 climate talks end without consensus on how to fund vulnerable countries or move the world away from coal, oil and gas use</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:66d1b9c76ca7b4f29f5427d364dc29128f927d96ba0218b2519d83d6a2ca0524</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:32Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T13:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cop31-climate-talks-end-without-consensus-on-how-to-fund-vulnerable-countries-or-move-the-world-away/a-80003610--d912dc284aaa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cop31-climate-talks-end-without-consensus-on-how-to-fund-vulnerable-countries-or-move-the-world-away-from-coal-oil-and-gas-use/a-80003610?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After two weeks of tough talks, the COP31 climate summit has closed without a consensus on how to quit fossil fuels or fund countries struggling to adapt to a hotter world.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>COP31: Climate deal 'not adopted,' summit president says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:db368272f761f530843b5ebf30aec9886dbb75893b5375c9d66e7eca1a1d802c</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:32Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T12:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cop31-climate-deal-not-adopted-summit-president-says/live-79999516--d760f7d7f78d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cop31-climate-deal-not-adopted-summit-president-says/live-79999516?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The summit was extended as nations worked to reach a deal, but they couldn't agree on including fossil fuels. European nations, small island states and activists have criticized oil-producing countries for the impasse.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Bayern Munich bosses under fire over Jamal Musiala comments</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c5b57167d7e95e42bfd97a7a9eba8c8f6e837fee7f60a0def2e2171a59f58e1e</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:32Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T11:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-bosses-under-fire-over-jamal-musiala-comments/a-80013187--78383bcfae5b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-bosses-under-fire-over-jamal-musiala-comments/a-80013187?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Officials have publicly questioned whether Musiala will ever fully recover from a debilitating neurological condition and queried the validity of his contract, prompting criticism from fans, media and the FIFPRO union.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>China, ASEAN countries struggle over South China Sea code of conduct</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:22c2770fafd2037ff5d408a912ea7d91b1169ec221830c4bfb00893ac2c308cf</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:32Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T08:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-asean-countries-struggle-over-south-china-sea-code-of-conduct/a-80009799--a3492edf3810.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-asean-countries-struggle-over-south-china-sea-code-of-conduct/a-80009799?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Philippines wanted a South China Sea code of conduct in place by 2026. But persistent disagreements between China and ASEAN countries are slowing progress toward a deal.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Inspired by Bernie Sanders: A German agency is using US-Style campaigning to boost the left in 2029</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2ed3952987dfd45f4c42d48d309d00d3f58fe16b8c310542bd62485d8fdf49f9</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:32Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T08:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/inspired-by-bernie-sanders-a-german-agency-is-using-us-style-campaigning-to-boost-the-left-in-2029/a-80001443--f6cd4061ee72.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/inspired-by-bernie-sanders-a-german-agency-is-using-us-style-campaigning-to-boost-the-left-in-2029/a-80001443?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">"The Goodforces" wants to see a swing to the left in the 2029 German elections. The agency counts New York Mayor Zohran Mamdani and Bernie Sanders among its inspirations. Could it transform the political landscape?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: IG Metall union calls for new 24-hour strike</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f5878253fc19e881f6c2b7f8fcca58aecddb295d8e1ce970bc8c675dce69fc0b</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:32Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T08:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-ig-metall-union-calls-for-new-24-hour-strike/live-80008430--32c896775229.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-ig-metall-union-calls-for-new-24-hour-strike/live-80008430?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's biggest single union, IG Metall, is calling on car and shipyard workers to strike amid a pay row. Meanwhile, Germany's president is setting off on an Africa trip. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US: ICE arrests 2 at Seattle airport in 'chilling' scenes — governor</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:95d6507e5f8be8fce8b362f6dc920fde8483e5946c0f32700fb1f8cc7335030c</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:32Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T07:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-ice-arrests-2-at-seattle-airport-in-chilling-scenes-governor/a-80012480--94de32aa4552.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-ice-arrests-2-at-seattle-airport-in-chilling-scenes-governor/a-80012480?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Washington's governor has denounced the arrests made by ICE officers at Seattle's airport, calling the incident "horrific."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India: Nepal PM Balendra Shah heads to Delhi for first bilateral visit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:15c1c0cc24d80c50ba98bc6a2653e6ab1a63cbd58cf9558a2d69f3d92026275b</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:32Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T07:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-nepal-pm-balendra-shah-heads-to-delhi-for-first-bilateral-visit/live-80008104--4f17524b4e9e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-nepal-pm-balendra-shah-heads-to-delhi-for-first-bilateral-visit/live-80008104?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nepal's rapper-turned-prime minister Balendra Shah is in New Delhi for his first foreign bilateral trip since taking office. He is expected to discuss flood recovery, trade and energy in his talks with Modi. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Dozens missing as deadly fire hits Indonesian candy factory</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:69d326ab4b775ba9815f395c51006d11cf21e0ea99b8233d451027263e30ce7a</id><updated>2026-11-23T07:54:32Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T06:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/dozens-missing-as-deadly-fire-hits-indonesian-candy-factory/a-80012342--07c7cd5dbdea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/dozens-missing-as-deadly-fire-hits-indonesian-candy-factory/a-80012342?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At least three people were killed in a devastating fire at a confectionery factory on Java. Officials said many more people remain unaccounted for, prompting fears of a much larger tragedy.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><en